A||||6||Dale||scrapping the computer
Z||000000||Dale||09-01-99||02:29 AM||||I would really like to get rid of the stock computer in my 84 SE.  Does anyone know if thier is another system to use and what else does the computer control besides engine functions.  I have an 85 K10  blazer w/350 I yanked out the computer in it and went to basics.  I got more power  and increased milage by about 3mpg.  Would love to do the same to the fiero
Z||000001||PaUL||09-01-99||12:19 PM||||hey Dale, the computer controls the fuel injection so you cant get rid of it without changing a lot of parts. Youd have to switch to a standalone throttle body FI system which I do think is available. Also youd need to switch to an older distributor that isnt controlled by the computer.
Z||000002||theogre||09-01-99||12:38 PM||||the biggest problem in the 84 motor isn't the computer. That whole version of the motor is weaker.<p>That version uses a flat lifter setup. This was changed to rollers in 86. You could upgrade to the rollers durring a rebuild.<p>That version uses the 600 TBI. It can be replaced with one from Holley that has increased air flow.<p>
Z||000003||Dale||09-01-99||05:25 PM||||Ya I knew that I would have to replace some things like the TBI and the distributer.  I was hoping that someone would know Of an aftermarket system for the fiero.  I know that there are some TBI systems that utylize an o2 sensor for other applications.  Is there another HEI dis. that will work in this motor without the computer? <p>And by the way Paul it's no fair, you have longer roads and speed limits higher than 50
Z||000004||PaUL||09-01-99||05:36 PM||||I dont know about the 2.5 4cycl but Im using a dist. from a 1980 citation which runs standalone without any connection to the ECM. I took it out of a citation I found abandoned in a sugar cane field. <p>And Dale, the roads here arent much longer, it would take me about 4 hours to circle the whole island.
Z||000005||Dale||09-01-99||06:55 PM||||It takes me about 1.5 hours to go from one end to the other.  It would probably take about 45 minutes if it weren't for all the small towns here.  I just happen to know where a citation is ( ofcourse its also in cane field)  I thought I almost had another fiero too.  Someone left it on the side of the road for 6 days, a 2m4.  I can't believe it didnt get touched.  I am guessing that the dis. is HEI and do you like it better than the computer?
Z||000006||PaUL||09-02-99||01:08 PM||||yes its an HEI with coil in the cap. I had no choice to use it because I swapped in a 2.8 from an 85 Celebrity which had a ECM controlled dist. Its ok but I just recently discovered that they came with different vac advance depending on the transmission. I got to get me one for a manual trans since I got the dist out of an automatic car.
